      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the Lagos gig worker, incorporating local iconography related to mobile money or known market operations can build trust more effectively than generic bright colors alone; clear, simple vernacular language within the UI also signals localization. Regarding the Dubai professional, expecting a \"corporate\" feel naturally implies a visual language of prestige—think refined typography, highly polished micro-interactions, and premium material design elements to signal status and reliability. Unlike the student, this user expects the UI to validate their high professional standing, so subtlety in luxury, not just flashiness, is key to perceived credibility.",
      "source": "target",
